  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A$, $B$, and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{C}{x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)$ gives\n\n$$\n5=(Ax+B)(x+2)+C({x}^{2}+4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =C(4+4) \\\\ 5 & =8C \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(0)+B)(0+2)+\\frac{5}{8}((0)^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =2B+\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 2B & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ B & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(1)+\\frac{5}{4})(1+2)+\\frac{5}{8}((1)^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =3A+\\frac{15}{4}+\\frac{25}{8} \\\\ 3A & =-\\frac{15}{8} \\\\ A & =-\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{5}{8}x+\\frac{5}{4})}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{(\\frac{5}{8})}{x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\,x+10}{8({x}^{2}+4)}+\\frac{5}{8(x+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
